00:15:32,880 --> 00:15:35,520
How can you forget your
boyfriend so quick?

249
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:38,800
I beg you, you don't hook
up with that bastard!

250
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:41,320
You know who I am!

251
00:15:43,300 --> 00:15:45,160
Let go of me!

252
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:47,310
No!

253
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:50,160
No, don't!

254
00:15:55,900 --> 00:15:57,380
This is absurd!

255
00:15:57,900 --> 00:15:59,620
Unhand me, you fiends!

256
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:01,180
I'm a human!

257
00:16:06,440 --> 00:16:09,220
Give me a ride, Onepoco! Not a chance!

258
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:11,087
You're way too heavy for me!

259
00:16:17,620 --> 00:16:23,357
I'll have a word with him don't worry

260
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:26,620
about him he's a toy just like us well

261
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:32,337
tell him who

262
00:16:32,420 --> 00:16:38,997
you are I'm the

263
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:40,786
father of that boy over there

264
00:16:41,100 --> 00:16:42,917
That woman with him is my wife.

265
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,180
My name is Milo, not one Poco.

266
00:16:48,740 --> 00:16:50,681
Young man, is your father around?

267
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,070
Nuh-uh.

268
00:16:52,153 --> 00:16:53,235
I never had one, sir.

269
00:16:54,020 --> 00:16:56,520
May I ask if you have a husband? I don't.

270
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:58,260
You see, I never married.

271
00:16:58,720 --> 00:17:00,380
Uh, is that so unusual?

272
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:03,410
Bye!

273
00:17:08,320 --> 00:17:09,277
A soldier?

274
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:12,837
What were you trying to prove
to me back there with the dog?

275
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:14,180
What's going on here?

276
00:17:16,700 --> 00:17:17,530
Simple.

277
00:17:17,820 --> 00:17:19,173
This kingdom's divided.

278
00:17:20,140 --> 00:17:24,740
A country filled with the forgotten,
and those who forget them.

279
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:30,280
Every toy you see was
at one point a human.

280
00:17:31,740 --> 00:17:32,570
What?!

281
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:38,237
Someone came to our island ten
years ago, courtesy of Doflamingo.

282
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:41,597
They turned us into toys
with their Devil Fruit power.

283
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:44,457
Wait, if you're a toy,

284
00:17:44,540 --> 00:17:48,897
that means look—we're
approaching flower field!

285
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:51,237
I'll tell you everything once we arrive.

286
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:52,150
No

287
00:18:02,900 --> 00:18:04,277
mercy for the wicked.

288
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:06,537
It'd be quicker if I wasn't a thun.

289
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:11,537
thun What are

290
00:18:11,620 --> 00:18:16,280
you waiting for, Nami?

291
00:18:17,660 --> 00:18:19,484
You were attacked, weren't you?

292
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:26,240
It's useless Haki!

293
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:29,837
We need tension rods to keep all
the shelves from falling down.

294
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:32,160
Say, Leo, you should get going soon.

295
00:18:32,540 --> 00:18:33,716
Do you need a lunch?

296
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:37,297
Thanks, Grandma, but I'm sure there'll
be something to eat over at headquarters.

297
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:38,320
If you're sure.

298
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:41,750
Careful!

299
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:43,250
I know.

300
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:46,242
I'm going to sew everything
that might fall over.

301
00:18:54,020 --> 00:18:54,850
There!

302
00:18:54,980 --> 00:18:56,333
Safety's been restored!

303
00:18:57,540 --> 00:19:00,260
Boy, that Usalund sure
is something, isn't he?

304
00:19:00,460 --> 00:19:05,157
So much power, he can shake the entire
kingdom only using that strange old Haki.

305
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:06,070
That's right!

306
00:19:06,153 --> 00:19:09,077
Because Usalund's a hero
straight out of the legends!

307
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:13,700
Oh, and by the way, Leo, I know I look
old, but I'm not going to topple over.

308
00:19:18,940 --> 00:19:20,657
So this is Tomtada Kingdom.

309
00:19:20,740 --> 00:19:23,217
What kind of relationship
do you think these

310
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:25,917
guys have with the
warlord Doflamingo anyway?

311
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:29,529
No clue, but I know they're
dead serious about fighting him.

312
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:32,101
Hey there, Usalind and Robbalind!

313
00:19:32,340 --> 00:19:34,340
Have you two gotten enough to eat?

314
00:19:35,180 --> 00:19:37,100
Oh, yeah, I totally pigged out.

315
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:41,468
Uh, that is, I am full
and ready for action!

316
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:45,231
See, what did I tell you?

317
00:19:45,460 --> 00:19:47,717
My body's trembling
with so much excitement,

318
00:19:47,800 --> 00:19:50,271
it's making the Earth shake all around us!

319
00:19:50,460 --> 00:19:51,290
Whoa!

320
00:19:51,373 --> 00:19:52,203
How awesome is that?

321
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:54,140
His power is off the charts.

322
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,440
One question, Leo.

323
00:19:57,760 --> 00:20:02,097
Your people keep mentioning some final
battle involving yours truly. But...

324
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:05,520
what reason do you want
to fight Doflamingo? Huh?

325
00:20:08,580 --> 00:20:11,000
Not just a hero, but a comedian, too.

326
00:20:11,220 --> 00:20:14,037
Because we want to rescue
500 of our closest friends.

327
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:16,777
Over in the secret factory in Dressrosa.

328
00:20:16,860 --> 00:20:18,417
where they're being enslaved, of course.

329
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:19,330
What?

330
00:20:19,413 --> 00:20:20,574
Did you say a factory?

331
00:20:20,860 --> 00:20:23,977
You mean the one Luffy and
the others want to destroy?

332
00:20:24,060 --> 00:20:25,037
Hey, wait a minute.

333
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:27,238
The same one that's producing Smile?

334
00:20:28,420 --> 00:20:31,277
I don't know what they're being
forced to manufacture there,

335
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:33,948
but they've imprisoned
an important tentata.

336
00:20:34,260 --> 00:20:36,789
Our obnoxious, selfish,
fickle, despicable,

337
00:20:36,940 --> 00:20:40,617
mean-spirited Princess Monchery
is being held inside that plant.

338
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:42,440
So we've got to hurry. Yeah?

339
00:20:42,620 --> 00:20:45,337
The way you describe her
makes her sound kind of awful.

340
00:20:45,420 --> 00:20:46,400
Oh, she is.

341
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:48,320
But she's still one of us.

342
00:20:49,860 --> 00:20:53,919
And Nolan himself would rescue anyone
who needed saving, wouldn't he?

343
00:20:54,780 --> 00:20:55,610
What? Right!

344
00:20:56,220 --> 00:20:58,477
That's totally what a real hero would do!

345
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:00,860
I mean, I am his descendant, after all!

346
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:04,940
Let's hear it for our legendary hero!

347
00:21:08,260 --> 00:21:09,300
Leo! Flopper!

348
00:21:10,540 --> 00:21:13,658
I heard the Don Quixote
family is leaving the palace!

349
00:21:14,420 --> 00:21:16,360
Probably beneath the Coliseum!

350
00:21:17,180 --> 00:21:21,460
The Yellow Cobbis and Beyond's pink
bees are ready to fly any time!

351
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:22,910
Understood!

352
00:21:25,820 --> 00:21:28,980
Let's move out, Usaland and Roboland! Huh?

353
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:32,260
Are the rest of you Tontadas ready to go?

354
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:36,700
Our fight is in Dressrosa!

355
00:21:36,840 --> 00:21:39,620
Beneath the Coliseum, inside the Factory!

356
00:21:40,140 --> 00:21:41,680
Everyone, go!

357
00:21:42,900 --> 00:21:43,730
Yeah!
